    intro: "Today we pause to remember. We learned that Christ is the resurrection and the life, that death is an enemy defeated by Christ, that believers who die are with him, that the unbelieving dead are in God's hands and will be judged, that Christ is the firstfruits of the resurrection, that our bodies will be raised and transformed, that the Old Testament hoped in God's faithfulness beyond death, that Christ will return, that God judges justly, that believers are justified by faith and will give an account of their service, and that all will stand before him.",
    context: "The first half of the course laid the foundations of death, resurrection and judgment. The test helps teachers and learners see what has been understood and what needs more attention. The second half will address hell and differing views, hard questions, heaven and the new creation, rewards, grief and funerals, facing one's own death, popular ideas about the afterlife, living with eternity in view and a personal plan.",
